:name: HWA10 update path
:description: The WPP pipe run with the boot chain that applies a pending bank:
:  the MBR hands control to the bootloader at 0xfc000, which copies the bank the
:  application downloaded into internal flash, and the application is re-patched
:  on the way in.

include @machine.resc
# Where this run hooks the application and what it re-applies after the update;
# abi/sim_patches.py rewrites it for a layout that moved the text.
include @moved-patches.resc

# UICR.NRFFW[0] holds the bootloader start address the MBR reads, and boot.resc
# leaves it erased so the MBR forwards to the SoftDevice. This run arms it only
# for the reboot that has a bank to apply: the bootloader compares the whole
# 1.15 MB bank against internal flash one SPI byte at a time, so taking that
# path on every boot costs minutes per boot, and the sim's own patches make
# internal flash differ from the bank by construction, so the comparison would
# never settle.

# CMD_RESTART_TO_UPDATE's handler (0x6ca44) is the moment the application asks
# for the bank to be applied: arm the hand-off so the reboot it is about to
# cause lands in the bootloader.
cpu AddHook 0x6ca44 'machine.SystemBus.WriteDoubleWord(0x10001014, 0xfc000)'

# The bootloader's reset entry. It reads POWER.RESETREAS to decide whether the
# RAM control block the application filled in survived; the sim has no reset
# cause to report, and every reset that reaches the bootloader here came from
# SYSRESETREQ, which is bit 2.
cpu AddHook 0xfc920 'monitor.Parse("sysbus.clock ResetReason 4")'

# The application's reset entry. The bootloader has just overwritten internal
# flash with the bank, so the sim's patches are gone and the protected-region
# reference is stale; moved-patches.resc's postUpdate restores both and disarms
# the hand-off so the next ordinary reboot goes straight to the SoftDevice.
cpu AddHook $appReset 'monitor.Parse("runMacro $postUpdate")'

# main init sleeps vTaskDelay(30001) before bringing up the UI (0x91faa,
# `movw r0, #0x7531`); make that 2001 ticks so the link is usable sooner.
sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0x91faa 0x70D1F240

logLevel -1 sysbus.wppPipe
emulation SetAdvanceImmediately true
sysbus.wppPipe Attach
start
